SUMMARY:Hebrew day 20: Numbers and money / Αριθμοί και χρήμα
 τα
DESCRIPTION:ah-KHAT es-REH  =  Έντεκα  /  Eleven\nes-REEM  =  Είκ
 οσι  /  Twenty\nshloh-SHEEM  =  Τριάντα  /  Thirty\nar-bah-EEM  
 =  Σαράντα  /  Forty\nkhah-mee-SHEEM  =  Πενήντα  /  Fifty\n
 meh-AH  =  Εκατό  /  Hundred\nEH-lef  =  Χίλια  /  Thousand\nSHE
 H-kel  =  Σέκελ  /  Shekel (Israeli money)\n\nSentence: zeh oh-LEH es
 -REEM SHEH-kel.\n= Κάνει είκοσι σέκελ.\n\nTip: Tens are th
 e small number + “-eem”: shalosh → shloshim. 25 = esrim ve-chamesh (
 twenty and five).\n\n(CAPS = stressed syllable\, kh = Greek χ)
