SUMMARY:Hebrew day 22: Shopping / Ψώνια
DESCRIPTION:leek-NOHT  =  Να αγοράσω  /  To buy\nyah-KAR  =  Ακ
 ριβό  /  Expensive\nZOHL  =  Φτηνό  /  Cheap\nmeev-TSAH  =  Πρ
 οσφορά  /  Special offer / sale\nkar-TEES ash-RAI  =  Πιστωτι
 κή κάρτα  /  Credit card\nmeh-zoo-MAHN  =  Μετρητά  /  Cash\
 nsah-KEET  =  Σακούλα  /  Bag\nef-SHAR …?  =  Γίνεται …\
 ; / Μπορώ να έχω …\;  /  May I have …? / Is it possible …?
 \n\nSentence: ef-SHAR leh-shah-LEM beh-kar-TEES?\n= Μπορώ να πλη
 ρώσω με κάρτα\;\n\nTip: “Efshar” is the most useful word in
  Israel: efshar mayim? efshar ha-cheshbon?\n\n(CAPS = stressed syllable\, 
 kh = Greek χ)
