SUMMARY:Hebrew day 24: Yesterday: I did / Αόριστος: έκανα
DESCRIPTION:hah-YEE-tee  =  Ήμουν  /  I was\nhah-LAKH-tee  =  Πήγα
   /  I went\nah-KHAL-tee  =  Έφαγα  /  I ate\nshah-TEE-tee  =  Ήπι
 α  /  I drank\nrah-EE-tee  =  Είδα  /  I saw\nah-MAR-tee  =  Είπα
   /  I said\nah-SEE-tee  =  Έκανα  /  I did / made\nshah-MAH-tee  =  
 Άκουσα  /  I heard\n\nSentence: et-MOHL hah-YEE-tee bah-YAHM.\n= Χ
 θες ήμουν στη θάλασσα.\n\nTip: Past tense “I” always
  ends in “-tee”\, just like Greek aorist ends in “-α” (πήγα\,
  έφαγα). Same for men and women.\n\n(CAPS = stressed syllable\, kh = 
 Greek χ)
