SUMMARY:Hebrew day 25: Tomorrow: I will / Μέλλοντας: θα
DESCRIPTION:ah-NEE eh-LEKH  =  Θα πάω  /  I will go\nah-NEE ah-VOH  = 
  Θα έρθω  /  I will come\nah-NEE ah-dah-BER  =  Θα μιλήσω  /
   I will speak\nah-NEE oh-KHAL  =  Θα φάω  /  I will eat\nah-NEE eh-Y
 EH  =  Θα είμαι  /  I will be\nah-NEE ek-NEH  =  Θα αγοράσ
 ω  /  I will buy\nah-NEE akh-ZOHR  =  Θα γυρίσω  /  I will come b
 ack\nah-NEE et-kah-SHER  =  Θα τηλεφωνήσω  /  I will call (pho
 ne)\n\nSentence: mah-KHAR ah-NEE eh-LEKH lah-YAHM.\n= Αύριο θα πά
 ω στη θάλασσα.\n\nTip: Future “I” starts with an “e-” o
 r “a-” sound. Think of it as Hebrew's “θα”.\n\n(CAPS = stressed 
 syllable\, kh = Greek χ)
